---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, ANALYTICS } from '../data/site';

const path = '/privacy/';
const updated = '2026-10-07';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Astrae Oratio Wiki"
  description="How Astrae Oratio Wiki (astraeoratio.org) handles data: analytics, cookies, embedded videos and your choices."
  {path}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy', href: path },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <header class="page-head">
        <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="meta-line">Effective <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time></p>
      </header>

      <p>
        Astrae Oratio Wiki (“we”, astraeoratio.org) is a static, read-only fan site. There are no user accounts, comments or
        forms, and we never ask you for personal information. This page explains the limited data that is processed when you
        visit.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
      <p>We use analytics to understand which pages are useful and to improve the site:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> — privacy-friendly analytics that uses no cookies and stores no personal data. It
          records aggregate information such as page views, referring sites, country, device type and clicks on outbound
          links. The script is served from our own domain; events are processed by Plausible Insights OÜ in the EU.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong>{ANALYTICS.ga4Id ? '' : ' (when enabled)'} — sets first-party cookies (such as
          <code>_ga</code>) to measure visits and engagement. Google processes this data under its own
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>. You can opt out with the
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a> or by blocking
          cookies in your browser.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="embeds">Embedded videos</h2>
      <p>
        Official trailers are shown as a thumbnail image first. The YouTube player — served from youtube-nocookie.com — only
        loads after you click play. Loading the thumbnail contacts YouTube’s image servers (i.ytimg.com).
      </p>

      <h2 id="preferences">Local preferences</h2>
      <p>
        If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser’s local storage on your device. It is
        never sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and logs</h2>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs (such as IP address, browser type and the page requested) for
        security and reliability. We don’t use them to identify visitors.
      </p>

      <h2 id="links">Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to the official Astrae Oratio website, NC services, YouTube, X and press sites. Their privacy practices are their
        own.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
